{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.GradedFrobeniusHopf","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.GradedFrobeniusHopf","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CategoricalFoundations","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.Instanton","lean:module:QOU.RepresentationTheory","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category"],"declarations":27,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.degree_geq1_dim_five","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.degree_geq1_dim_five","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GradedFrobeniusHopf.lean#L171-L174","doc":"The degree-≥1 subspace has dimension 5 (standard × 2 + alternating). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.graded_pieces_exhaust_h3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.graded_pieces_exhaust_h3","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GradedFrobeniusHopf.lean#L162-L169","doc":"The two graded pieces exhaust `H₃(q)`: the degree-0 subspace\n(`degreeZeroDim`) together with the degree-≥1 subspace (dimension 5,\n`degree_geq1_dim_five`) account for all `3! = 6` dimensions.  False\nfor any other degree-0 dimension, so the constant is load-bearing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.degreeZeroDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.degreeZeroDim","kind":"def","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GradedFrobeniusHopf.lean#L151-L160","doc":"The dimension of the degree-0 subspace (the symmetric eigenspace).\nA **named constant**, not a theorem.\n\nReplaced `theorem degree_zero_dim_one : (1 : ℕ) = 1 := rfl`\n(2026-08-21; vacuity ledger, `reflexive-tautology-ascribed-literal`).\n`1 = 1` holds whatever that dimension is, so the statement asserted\nnothing about the graded piece; per Strict Lean Discipline §8 a claim\nwith no falsifiable content is notation and belongs in a `def`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.hecke_h3_wedderburn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.hecke_h3_wedderburn","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GradedFrobeniusHopf.lean#L143-L149","doc":"The regular representation dimension identity for `H₃(q)`:\n`dim(V_sym) + 2·dim(V_std) + dim(V_alt) = |S₃| = 6`.\n\nThis is the rank version of the Wedderburn-Artin decomposition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeIrrepDecomposition.total_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeIrrepDecomposition.total_dim","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GradedFrobeniusHopf.lean#L141-L141","doc":"Total dimension equals `|S₃| = 6`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeIrrepDecomposition.dim_alt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeIrrepDecomposition.dim_alt","kind":"def","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GradedFrobeniusHopf.lean#L139-L139","doc":"Dimension of alternating irrep. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeIrrepDecomposition.std_multiplicity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeIrrepDecomposition.std_multiplicity","kind":"def","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GradedFrobeniusHopf.lean#L137-L137","doc":"Multiplicity of standard irrep in the regular representation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeIrrepDecomposition.dim_std","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeIrrepDecomposition.dim_std","kind":"def","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GradedFrobeniusHopf.lean#L135-L135","doc":"Dimension of standard irrep. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeIrrepDecomposition.dim_sym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeIrrepDecomposition.dim_sym","kind":"def","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GradedFrobeniusHopf.lean#L133-L133","doc":"Dimension of symmetric irrep. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeIrrepDecomposition.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeIrrepDecomposition.mk","kind":"ctor","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GradedFrobeniusHopf.lean#L131-L131","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeIrrepDecomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeIrrepDecomposition","kind":"structure","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GradedFrobeniusHopf.lean#L117-L141","doc":"The **Hecke irrep decomposition** of `H₃(q)`.\n\nThe regular representation of `H₃(q)` decomposes as:\n`H₃(q) ≅ V_sym ⊕ V_std ⊕ V_std ⊕ V_alt`\nwith dimensions `1 + 2 + 2 + 1 = 6 = |S₃|`.\n\n- `V_sym`: the 1D symmetric representation (degree 0)\n- `V_std`: the 2D standard representation (degree 1), multiplicity 2\n- `V_alt`: the 1D alternating representation (top degree)\n\nThe graded Frobenius--Hopf decomposition restricts to:\n- Degree 0: `V_sym` (1D) — the vector coupling channel\n- Degree ≥ 1: `V_std ⊕ V_std ⊕ V_alt` (4D + 1D) — the axial coupling channel ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.adjoint_dim_implies_channel_separation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.adjoint_dim_implies_channel_separation","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GradedFrobeniusHopf.lean#L98-L113","doc":"**Corollary**: In `Rep(SU_q(2))`, `Ad(A) ≅ V₂` (spin-1, dimension 3),\nwhich has no trivial (spin-0) sub-object.\n\nThe categorical dimension confirms the channel separation:\n- `dim(Ad) = 3` (the spin-1 irreducible)\n- `dim(𝟙) = 1` (the trivial representation)\n- These are non-isomorphic simple objects → `Hom(𝟙, Ad) = 0`\n\nThis recovers the Bring's surface observability theorem. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SymDim1.symDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SymDim1.symDim","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GradedFrobeniusHopf.lean#L94-L94","doc":"The symmetric component is categorically 1-dimensional. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SymDim1.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SymDim1.mk","kind":"ctor","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GradedFrobeniusHopf.lean#L89-L89","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SymDim1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SymDim1","kind":"structure","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GradedFrobeniusHopf.lean#L87-L94","doc":"The degree-0 component has categorical dimension 1 (the trivial rep). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GradedFrobeniusHopf.sym_idempotent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GradedFrobeniusHopf.sym_idempotent","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GradedFrobeniusHopf.lean#L85-L85","doc":"**Idempotent (sym)**: `π_sym` is idempotent via the inclusion-projection\nfactorisation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GradedFrobeniusHopf.high_retraction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GradedFrobeniusHopf.high_retraction","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GradedFrobeniusHopf.lean#L82-L82","doc":"**Projection retraction (high)**: `π_high ∘ ι_high = id_{A₁}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GradedFrobeniusHopf.sym_retraction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GradedFrobeniusHopf.sym_retraction","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GradedFrobeniusHopf.lean#L80-L80","doc":"**Projection retraction (sym)**: `π_sym ∘ ι_sym = id_{A₀}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GradedFrobeniusHopf.highInclusion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GradedFrobeniusHopf.highInclusion","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GradedFrobeniusHopf.lean#L78-L78","doc":"The inclusion of the high-degree component `ι_high : A₁ ↪ A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GradedFrobeniusHopf.symInclusion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GradedFrobeniusHopf.symInclusion","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GradedFrobeniusHopf.lean#L76-L76","doc":"The inclusion of the symmetric component `ι_sym : A₀ ↪ A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GradedFrobeniusHopf.highProjection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GradedFrobeniusHopf.highProjection","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GradedFrobeniusHopf.lean#L74-L74","doc":"The complementary projection `π_high : A → A₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GradedFrobeniusHopf.symProjection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GradedFrobeniusHopf.symProjection","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GradedFrobeniusHopf.lean#L72-L72","doc":"The symmetrizer projection `π_sym : A → A₀`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GradedFrobeniusHopf.highComponent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GradedFrobeniusHopf.highComponent","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GradedFrobeniusHopf.lean#L70-L70","doc":"The degree-≥1 component of `A`.\nCarries the standard and alternating representations. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GradedFrobeniusHopf.symComponent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GradedFrobeniusHopf.symComponent","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GradedFrobeniusHopf.lean#L67-L67","doc":"The degree-0 (symmetric) component of `A`.\nIsomorphic to `Hom(𝟙, A)` — the space of invariant elements. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GradedFrobeniusHopf.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GradedFrobeniusHopf.mk","kind":"ctor","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GradedFrobeniusHopf.lean#L63-L63","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GradedFrobeniusHopf.toFrobeniusHopfData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GradedFrobeniusHopf.toFrobeniusHopfData","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GradedFrobeniusHopf.lean#L63-L85","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GradedFrobeniusHopf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GradedFrobeniusHopf","kind":"structure","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/GradedFrobeniusHopf.lean#L48-L85","doc":"**Graded Frobenius--Hopf object**: the Frobenius--Hopf object `A`\nequipped with a decomposition into degree-0 (symmetric) and\ndegree-≥1 (standard + alternating) components.\n\nThe grading comes from the Iwahori--Hecke algebra filtration:\n- Degree 0: image of the Young symmetric idempotent `e_{(n)}`\n- Degree ≥ 1: kernel of the symmetrizer projection\n\nIn `Rep(SU_q(2))`:\n- Degree 0 ↔ trivial representation `𝟙` (dim 1, spin 0)\n- Degree 1 ↔ standard representation `V₂` (dim 2, spin ½)\n- Top degree ↔ alternating representation (dim 1, spin equivalent)\n\nLaTeX: new definition supporting `\\label{def:graded-frobenius-hopf}` ","signatureChunk":0}]}